From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:06:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: Keep oob_notify at the end of drm_bridge_funcs

"drm/bridge: Add out-of-band HPD notify handler" inserts the new
oob_notify callback in the middle of struct drm_bridge_funcs, which
shifts the offsets of all HDMI, DP audio and debugfs callbacks after it.

On the Orange Pi 5 kernel DRM core, the KMS helpers and the panel bridge
are built in, while the display helpers (bridge connector), the DW DP
bridge and rockchipdrm are modules. To be able to test the USB-C DP
AltMode stack by replacing just those modules on top of an existing
7.3 kernel image, the layout of the structure seen by the built-in code
must not change. Move the new callback to the end of the structure; it
is only called from drm_bridge_connector.c.

This is a local change for the out-of-tree port and has no upstream
equivalent; drop it when rebasing onto a kernel with the upstream patch.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 include/drm/drm_bridge.h | 31 +++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/drm/drm_bridge.h b/include/drm/drm_bridge.h
index 713652fca033..a2b99ed24a1d 100644
--- a/include/drm/drm_bridge.h
+++ b/include/drm/drm_bridge.h
@@ -540,20 +540,6 @@ struct drm_bridge_funcs {
 	 */
 	void (*hpd_disable)(struct drm_bridge *bridge);
 
-	/**
-	 * @oob_notify:
-	 *
-	 * Notify the bridge of out of band hot plug detection.
-	 *
-	 * This callback is optional, it may be implemented by bridges that
-	 * need to be notified of display connection or disconnection for
-	 * internal reasons. One use case is to force the DP controllers HPD
-	 * signal for USB-C DP AltMode.
-	 */
-	void (*oob_notify)(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
-			   struct drm_connector *connector,
-			   enum drm_connector_status status);
-
 	/**
 	 * @hdmi_tmds_char_rate_valid:
 	 *
@@ -866,6 +852,23 @@ struct drm_bridge_funcs {
 	 * Allows bridges to create bridge-specific debugfs files.
 	 */
 	void (*debugfs_init)(struct drm_bridge *bridge, struct dentry *root);
+
+	/**
+	 * @oob_notify:
+	 *
+	 * Notify the bridge of out of band hot plug detection.
+	 *
+	 * This callback is optional, it may be implemented by bridges that
+	 * need to be notified of display connection or disconnection for
+	 * internal reasons. One use case is to force the DP controllers HPD
+	 * signal for USB-C DP AltMode.
+	 *
+	 * Keep this at the end of the structure: it is only used by modular
+	 * code, so appending it keeps the layout seen by built-in code intact.
+	 */
+	void (*oob_notify)(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
+			   struct drm_connector *connector,
+			   enum drm_connector_status status);
 };
 
 /**
